        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Jurchens</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Homeland</span><span class="info-stat-val">the forests and river valleys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heilongjiang">Heilongjiang</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jilin">Jilin provinces</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s Primorsky Krai; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudan-river">Mudan River</a>, the Changbai mountains, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a>, the Songhua and Amur rivers and the Yalu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tumen">Tumen</a> borderlands</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">first in Chinese records in 748; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a> by the 11th century; the Wanyan federation under Wugunai (1021–74); the Jin dynasty (1115–1234); Jianzhou, Haixi and Wild Jurchens under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming dynasty</a> (1368–1644); unification under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nurhaci">Nurhaci</a> from 1586; renamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchus</a> in 1635</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the Jin dynasty and the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> in 1127; the Jurchen script of 1120; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eight-banners">Eight Banners</a>; the queue hairstyle; horsemanship, archery and hunting; trade in pearls and ginseng; founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing dynasty</a></span></div>
